  "raw_text": "312\n\nVERB IRREGULARITIES / IRREGULARIDADES VERBALES\n\nVERBS WITH ROOT THAT ENDS IN “B”\n \n…………………..\n\nThe\n \nletter “b” is removed from the conjugation in 5 forms of the verg\n. /\n\nLa letra “b”\ns\ne elimina de la conjugación\n \nen 5 formas del verbo.\n\nExamples\n \nusing\n \nUlbaia\n \n/\n \nEjemplos\n \nusando\n \nUlbaia\n:\n\n2\nnd\n \nperson Future II / 2\ndo\n \npersona Futuro II:\n \nUlma\n \n(\nUlbma\n);\n\n3\nrd\n \nperson Future II /\n \n3\ner\n \npersona Futuro II:\n \nUlbia\n \n(\nUlbbia\n);\n\nProhibitive/Prohibitiva:\n \nUlpara\n \n(\nUlbpara\n);\n\nImperative/Imperativa:\n \nUls\n \n(\nUlbs\n);\n\n3\nrd\n \nperson connective / 3\ner\n \npersona conexivo:\n \nUlka\n \n(\nUlbka\n);\n\nVERBS WITH ROOT THAT ENDS IN “\nSW\n”\n \n…\n(also checking nw, hw, kw, mw, gw, lw, rw, tw, and maybe other\nconsonants)..\n\nDaswaia\n \n–\n \n3p fut\n \n–\n \nDasbia\n \n(Daswbia)\n\n”A” to “I”\n\nDawan Bila (\ndb\n)\n \n–\n \nOften replaces the letter “\na\n” in verb conjugations with an “\ni\n”\n \n/\n\nA menudo reemplaza la letra \"\na\n\" en\n \nconjugaciones verbales con una \"\ni\n\"\n\nExamples/Ejemplos:\n\nAisan\n \n→\n \nAisin\n\nSna\n \n→\n \nSni\n\nBrisna\n \n→\n \nBrisni\n\nPahbamna\n \n→\n \nPahbamni\n\nOTHER IRREGULARITIES\n\nAisaia\n \n–\n \nWhen conjugated,\n \nhas an “\na\n” added after the root\n \nin the following cases: /\n\nCuando se conjuga, se\n \nagrega una \"\na\n\" después de la raíz en los siguientes casos\n:\n\nAisama\n \n(\nAisma\n);\n \nAisabia\n \n(\nAisbia\n);\n \nAisaras\n \n(\nAisras\n);\n \nAisari\n \n(\nAisri\n);\n \nAisaram\n \n(\nAisram\n);\n \nAisapara\n \n(\nAispara\n);\n \nAisas\n\n(\nAis\ns\n).\n\nKaikaia\n \n–\n \nIn addition to the regular imperative form:\n \nKaiks\n, there is an alternative form:\n \nKais\n\nAdemás de la forma imperativa regular:\n \nKaiks\n, hay una forma alternativa:\n \nKais\n\nPruaia\n \n–\n \nPruna\n \n(\nPruuna\n)\n;\n \nPruma\n \n(\nPruuma\n)\n;\n \nPruya\n \n(\nPruuya\n)\n\nYaia\n \n–\n \nPresent/Presente 2:\n \nIsna\n \n(\nYisna\n)\n;\n \nIsma\n \n(\nYisma\n)\n \n;\n \nIsa\n \n(\nYisa\n)\n\n–\n \nPast/Pasado 2:\n \nYari\n \n(\nY\nri\n)\n;\n \nYaram\n \n(\nY\nram\n)\n\n–\n \nFuture/Futuro 2:\n \nYama\n \n(\nY\nma\n)\n;\n \nYabia\n \n(\nY\nbia\n)\n\n–\n \nImperative/Imperativa:\n \nYas\n \n(\nYs\n)",
